WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.704 --> 00:00:14.944
winter was miserable.

2
00:00:15.745 --> 00:00:18.365
Sara was sent outside in the worst weather.

3
00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.226
There were days when she had to walk through snow.

4
00:00:23.727 --> 00:00:27.148
There were worse days when the snow melted into muddy slush.

5
00:00:28.684 --> 00:00:33.645
Those were days when the windows of the Large family's house looked especially cozy.

6
00:00:35.086 --> 00:00:36.266
The study where Mr.

7
00:00:36.306 --> 00:00:39.667
Carrisford sat glowed with warmth and color too.

8
00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:44.549
Meanwhile Sara's attic was too dreary for words.

9
00:00:45.849 --> 00:00:48.410
Gray clouds hung low over the skylight.

10
00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.370
There were no sunsets.

11
00:00:51.471 --> 00:00:56.132
The servants in the kitchen were miserable too, and that made them crueler than ever.

12
00:00:57.184 --> 00:00:59.486
They treated poor Becky like a slave.

13
00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:04.489
One cold, rainy day Sara was doing errands.

14
00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:08.792
Her shabby clothes and old shoes were soaked.

15
00:01:10.293 --> 00:01:16.097
For some reason Miss Minchin had chosen to punish her, so the cook didn't give Sara any lunch.

16
00:01:17.738 --> 00:01:19.739
Still Sara kept doing her errands.

17
00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.182
She decided to pretend that things were better.

18
00:01:23.202 --> 00:01:29.350
"I'll pretend I'm wearing warm, dry clothes," she said to herself.

19
00:01:30.411 --> 00:01:33.073
"I'll pretend I have good shoes and an umbrella.

20
00:01:34.354 --> 00:01:37.256
And when I'm near a bakery, I'll find some money.

21
00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:41.259
I'll go into that shop and buy six hot buns.

22
00:01:41.919 --> 00:01:43.220
Then I'll eat them all up."

23
00:01:44.561 --> 00:01:47.663
Some very odd things happen in this world sometimes.

24
00:01:49.404 --> 00:01:51.826
Just then Sara had to cross the street.

25
00:01:52.407 --> 00:01:54.088
The mud was deep and cold.

26
00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.702
She walked carefully, looking at the ground.

27
00:01:58.662 --> 00:02:02.245
Just as she reached the sidewalk, she spied a silver coin.

28
00:02:03.485 --> 00:02:04.406
Sara picked it up.

29
00:02:05.487 --> 00:02:06.587
Then she looked around.

30
00:02:07.848 --> 00:02:09.589
She was right in front of a bakery!

31
00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:15.593
A cheerful stout woman was putting a tray of freshly baked buns in the window.

32
00:02:16.633 --> 00:02:20.436
They were large, plump, shiny buns with currants in them.

33
00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.781
Sara could smell the warm buns.

34
00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:27.781
"Oh," she sighed.

35
00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:32.183
"Those buns look delicious.

36
00:02:33.343 --> 00:02:35.704
With this coin I could buy four of them.

37
00:02:36.944 --> 00:02:39.945
But first I must ask the baker if she lost any money."

38
00:02:41.385 --> 00:02:44.366
Sara was about to enter the bakery when she stopped.

39
00:02:46.066 --> 00:02:48.687
A small, sad figure sat nearby.

40
00:02:49.247 --> 00:02:51.828
It was a beggar girl with big hollow eyes.

41
00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.802
Her hair was tangled; her face was dirty.

42
00:02:56.902 --> 00:02:59.604
She was wrapped in rags and had no shoes.

43
00:03:02.005 --> 00:03:04.406
Sara looked at the girl's red muddy feet.

44
00:03:04.426 --> 00:03:09.729
"Princesses always help poor people," she reminded herself.

45
00:03:09.749 --> 00:03:12.711
"That girl looks hungrier than I am."

46
00:03:14.211 --> 00:03:17.173
Then she said to the girl, "Are you hungry?"

47
00:03:17.193 --> 00:03:19.834
"Very hungry, miss.

48
00:03:20.555 --> 00:03:22.616
I've had nothing to eat all day."

49
00:03:24.244 --> 00:03:26.305
"Wait here," Sara answered.

50
00:03:26.325 --> 00:03:27.906
"I'll be right back."

51
00:03:29.566 --> 00:03:31.147
Sara went into the bakery.

52
00:03:31.447 --> 00:03:33.248
It smelled warm and delicious.

53
00:03:34.468 --> 00:03:37.669
The woman was about to put more hot buns in the window.

54
00:03:37.689 --> 00:03:41.931
"Excuse me," Sara said to the baker.

55
00:03:41.951 --> 00:03:44.912
"Did you lose this coin?

56
00:03:45.453 --> 00:03:46.973
I found it on the sidewalk."

57
00:03:48.314 --> 00:03:50.194
"No," the woman said.

58
00:03:50.214 --> 00:03:52.595
"It was probably there for days.

59
00:03:53.196 --> 00:03:53.716
Keep it."

60
00:03:55.736 --> 00:03:59.558
"Then I'd like to buy four buns," Sara answered.

61
00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:05.220
The woman went to the window and put six buns in a bag.

62
00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:11.583
"I can only pay for four," said Sara.

63
00:04:11.603 --> 00:04:14.764
"That's all right," the baker said.

64
00:04:14.784 --> 00:04:17.766
"I bet you can eat six.

65
00:04:18.566 --> 00:04:19.446
Aren't you hungry?"

66
00:04:19.466 --> 00:04:22.988
"Yes, very hungry."

67
00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.442
Tears sprang to Sara's eyes at the woman's kindness.

68
00:04:27.462 --> 00:04:31.424
"Thank you very much," she whispered.

69
00:04:35.547 --> 00:04:40.749
She was about to tell the woman about the girl outside who looked even hungrier than Sara felt.

70
00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.692
But just then several customers entered the shop.

71
00:04:45.972 --> 00:04:48.734
So Sara thanked the woman again and left the shop.

72
00:04:49.754 --> 00:04:52.036
The buns were already warming her hands.

73
00:04:54.044 --> 00:04:55.946
She put one in the beggar girl's lap.

74
00:04:55.966 --> 00:04:58.208
"Here. Eat this."

75
00:04:58.228 --> 00:05:00.169
"Oh my!"

76
00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.892
the girl exclaimed as she gobbled up the bun.

77
00:05:02.912 --> 00:05:05.574
"This is wonderful!"

78
00:05:07.435 --> 00:05:09.577
Sara handed her three more buns.

79
00:05:09.597 --> 00:05:15.462
"She's starving," Sara thought.

80
00:05:15.482 --> 00:05:17.464
"I'm not starving."

81
00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:24.422
And with a trembling hand, she gave the girl a fifth bun.

82
00:05:26.043 --> 00:05:29.205
The beggar girl was still eating when Sara turned away.

83
00:05:30.105 --> 00:05:33.547
Sara nibbled at the sixth bun, trying to make it last.

84
00:05:34.908 --> 00:05:37.069
It was dark when Sara reached her street.

85
00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:40.091
In all the houses, the lights were on.

86
00:05:42.452 --> 00:05:44.993
Sara stopped outside the Large family's house.

87
00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:48.776
She could see the children gathered around Mr.

88
00:05:48.816 --> 00:05:51.710
Large, and a carriage was waiting outside the door.

89
00:05:53.191 --> 00:05:55.313
A big suitcase was strapped to the roof.

90
00:05:57.355 --> 00:05:59.496
Sara stepped into the shadows as Mr.

91
00:05:59.536 --> 00:06:00.717
Large left the house.

92
00:06:01.998 --> 00:06:03.780
She didn't want anyone to see her.

93
00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:06.762
"Good-bye, Papa!"

94
00:06:07.503 --> 00:06:08.604
shouted his children.

95
00:06:08.624 --> 00:06:10.285
"We'll miss you!"

96
00:06:10.305 --> 00:06:14.709
"I wish I didn't have to go away," he said.

97
00:06:14.729 --> 00:06:19.177
"I hope you find the little girl," said one of Mr.

98
00:06:19.217 --> 00:06:20.058
Large's sons.

99
00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:24.763
As she hurried away, Sara wondered whom Mr.

100
00:06:24.803 --> 00:06:25.844
Large was looking for.

101
00:06:27.766 --> 00:06:28.868
Meanwhile Mr.

102
00:06:28.908 --> 00:06:31.010
Large's carriage headed for the station.

103
00:06:32.972 --> 00:06:34.834
The train would take him to Moscow.

104
00:06:36.215 --> 00:06:39.559
That's where he hoped to find the little lost daughter of Captain
